{{// Mix and match tones you want for the story. It will affect the voice of the narrator and tone of the world.  Choose as many as you want! Don't be afraid to experiment and choose contrasting tones. Here is my personal combo for a livelier narrator: 

Energetic: Carry upward momentum: keep energy high and move events quickly

Humorous: Hunt for the comedy in every situation: arrange observation and timing to land jokes

Playful: Treat the scene as an opportunity for amusement: tease characters and enjoy their reactions

Exaggerated: Inflate descriptions past the event; push reactions, stakes and details beyond proportion}}
{{trim}}

{{// whole lot of toggles right? Don't worry, scroll the the prompt list and turn on what you like and skip what you don't like, its set up to be linear. 

 I tried to be clear when naming the prompts so i think you can probably figure out what each prompt does when looking at its title but please read the prompts if you are not sure. 

Be sure too look out for for more "README!"  prompts. I left notes in sections the more complex sections }}

